<title>USA: Briggs &amp; Stratton sells $100 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Briggs &amp; Stratton sells $100 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Briggs &amp; Stratton Corp was priced on Friday, according to lead manager Credit Suisse First Boston</p>
<p>Briggs &amp; Stratton is a Wisconsin-based manufacturer of small engines.</p>
<p>BORROWER BRIGGS &amp; STRATTON CORP</p>
<p>AMT $100 MLN	 COUPON 7.25 PCT   MATURITY 9/15/07</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.303  FIRST PAY DATE 3/15/98</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA2  YIELD 7.34 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB-PLUS  SPREAD +64 BPS    CALLABLE MAKE-WHOLE CALL AT</p>
<p>							    +15 BPS OVER US</p>
<p>							    TREASURIES</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
